---
import DefaultLayout from "@layouts/DefaultLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import { Heading } from "accessible-astro-components";
---

<DefaultLayout title="Code of Conduct">
  <PageHeader
    title="Code of Conduct"
    subtitle="The standards of behaviour and values required of all DUCA staff, committee, and executive members."
    bgType="bordered"
    customBreadcrumbLabels={{ "code-of-conduct": "Code of Conduct" }}
  />
  <section class="narrow container my-16">
    <div class="space-content">
      <Heading level="h2">1. Introduction</Heading>
      <p>
        This Code of Conduct sets out the standards of behaviour required of every person who holds a staff, committee, or executive role at the Deakin University Cybersecurity Association (DUCA). It applies from the moment a role is accepted and for the full duration of that role.
      </p>
      <p>
        DUCA exists to make cybersecurity accessible, welcoming, and valuable for all students. The way our team behaves, whether at events, online, or in day-to-day communications, directly shapes that experience for our members. This document protects members, protects our team, and protects the club.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reading and agreeing to this Code of Conduct is a condition of holding any leadership or staff role at DUCA.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">2. Who This Applies To</Heading>
      <p>
        Where this document uses the words "staff" or "team", it refers to all individuals holding roles within the following categories:
      </p>
      
      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Role Category</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Includes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Executive</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">President, Vice-President, Treasurer, Secretary, Assistant Secretary</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Team Leads</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Development TL, CTF TL, Presentation TL, Marketing TL</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">General Committee</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">All general committee members</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Advisors</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Club advisors in any capacity</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        Advisors are included in the conduct and values standards in this document. Operational requirements (such as event rostering obligations) apply to advisors only where they have accepted a specific operational commitment.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">3. Our Core Values</Heading>
      <p>
        These values are the baseline for every person who holds a staff role at DUCA. They are not optional.
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Value</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">What it means</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Inclusion</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Everyone belongs, regardless of background, identity, or experience level.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Respect</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Treat every person with dignity, in every context.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Accountability</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Own your responsibilities and your mistakes.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Reliability</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Follow through on what you commit to.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Leadership</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Step up when the situation calls for it.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h2">4. Respect and Inclusion</Heading>
      
      <Heading level="h3">4.1 Discrimination and Hate</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA has zero tolerance for discrimination, hate speech, or any conduct that targets a person or group based on:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Race or ethnicity</li>
        <li>Gender or gender identity</li>
        <li>Sexual orientation</li>
        <li>Religion or belief</li>
        <li>Disability</li>
        <li>Nationality or immigration status</li>
        <li>Age</li>
        <li>Socioeconomic background</li>
        <li>Any other characteristic that is part of who someone is</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This includes but is not limited to: racist remarks, sexist behaviour, homophobia, transphobia, ableism, xenophobia, and any other conduct intended to demean, exclude, or harm a person based on who they are.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-red-400 block mb-2">⚠️ Zero Tolerance Policy</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-red-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Conduct of this nature is treated as a serious breach and will result in immediate dismissal from the team. There is no warning threshold for hate-based conduct.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h3">4.2 Condescension and Disrespect</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA welcomes students at all experience levels. Staff must treat every person, including members, fellow staff, industry partners, and members of the public, with patience and respect. Condescension is not acceptable, regardless of how experienced you are or how basic the question is.
      </p>
      <p>This includes:</p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Talking down to members who are less experienced</li>
        <li>Making someone feel unwelcome for asking a question</li>
        <li>Dismissing another staff member's contribution in a meeting or channel</li>
        <li>Using sarcasm or humour that targets a specific person</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you would not say it to someone's face without it being hurtful, do not say it.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">4.3 Inclusive Language</Heading>
      <p>
        Staff must use language that is inclusive and respectful in all club contexts. This includes event scripts, internal messages, social media, and verbal communication at events. If you are unsure whether language you are using is appropriate, err on the side of caution and ask.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">5. Online Conduct</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">5.1 Personal Social Media</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA staff are expected to maintain personal social media conduct that is consistent with the values in this document. DUCA recognises that staff have personal lives and personal opinions. What is not acceptable is content that is hateful, discriminatory, or harmful.
      </p>
      <p>Staff must not post, share, like, or publicly engage with content that:</p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Promotes hatred or discrimination toward any person or group</li>
        <li>Harasses or targets an individual</li>
        <li>Promotes or glorifies violence</li>
        <li>Spreads misinformation in a way that harms others</li>
        <li>Is sexually explicit in a way that would embarrass the club or its members</li>
        <li>Undermines the reputation of DUCA, DUSA, or Deakin University</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-purple-500/30 bg-purple-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-purple-400 block mb-2">ℹ️ Scope of Platforms</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-purple-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          This applies to all platforms, including but not limited to Instagram, TikTok, X (formerly Twitter), LinkedIn, Reddit, Discord, Facebook, Snapchat, and any other public or semi-public forum.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h3">5.2 Political Content</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA does not align with any political party, candidate, or political movement. Staff must not:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Represent DUCA as aligned with any political party or ideological movement</li>
        <li>Use DUCA platforms to advance personal political views</li>
        <li>Publicly promote or share content from political parties or movements whose platform is built on hate, discrimination, or the removal of rights from any group of people</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This does not prevent staff from having personal political views. It means those views must be clearly kept separate from your role at DUCA.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">5.3 DUCA Platforms</Heading>
      <p>
        When posting or communicating on any DUCA-owned or DUCA-managed platform (including Instagram, LinkedIn, Discord, and any other official DUCA channel), staff must:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Represent the club professionally and inclusively</li>
        <li>Not post on behalf of DUCA without authorisation from the Marketing Team Lead or an Executive</li>
        <li>Not share internal club information or unconfirmed announcements publicly without approval</li>
      </ul>

      <Heading level="h2">6. Pre-Appointment Screening</Heading>
      <p>
        Before any person is offered a staff role at DUCA, the club reserves the right to conduct a social media review as part of the standard assessment process.
      </p>
      <p>
        This review is looking for conduct that would be inconsistent with this Code of Conduct, including but not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Hate speech or discriminatory content</li>
        <li>Harassment or targeting of individuals</li>
        <li>Content promoting violence or extreme ideologies</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This process is applied consistently and is not targeted at any individual characteristic.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-amber-400 block mb-2">⚠️ Integrity in Applications</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Dishonesty during the application process is grounds for immediate rejection or dismissal. If a candidate attempts to conceal or delete content in bad faith ahead of a review, and this is identified, the application will not proceed or the offer will be withdrawn. Applicants will be informed that a social media review may be conducted before any review takes place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Existing staff: If a concern is raised about a current staff member's social media conduct, DUCA reserves the right to review that conduct as part of a disciplinary inquiry under Section 15.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">7. Event Conduct</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">7.1 Intoxication and Substance Use</Heading>
      <p>
        No staff member may attend or assist with a DUCA event while under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that impairs their ability to perform their role safely and effectively.
      </p>
      <p>This includes:</p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Arriving at an event already intoxicated or otherwise impaired</li>
        <li>Consuming alcohol or substances during an event setup, running period, or pack-down</li>
        <li>Being in a state that poses a risk to your own safety or the safety of others</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-red-400 block mb-2">⚠️ Important Security Standard</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-red-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Breaching this rule is a serious breach. Depending on the circumstances, it will result in removal from the event and may result in immediate dismissal.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h3">7.2 Violence and Aggression</Heading>
      <p>
        Violence, physical aggression, and threatening behaviour have no place at DUCA. This includes:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Physical altercations of any kind</li>
        <li>Verbal aggression or threatening language directed at any person</li>
        <li>Intimidation, coercion, or conduct designed to make a person feel unsafe</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Any staff member who engages in violence or aggression at or in connection with a DUCA event will be removed immediately and may face immediate dismissal.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">7.3 Patience and Conduct with Members</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA events regularly attract students who are brand new to cybersecurity. Staff must remain patient, approachable, and welcoming at all times. If you are frustrated or overwhelmed, take a moment to collect yourself. Do not direct frustration toward members or attendees.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">7.4 Emergencies at Events</Heading>
      <p>If a safety emergency occurs at a DUCA event, staff must:</p>
      <ol class="list-inside list-decimal space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Prioritise the safety of attendees above all else</li>
        <li>Call 000 if there is an immediate threat to life or physical safety</li>
        <li>Contact an Executive team member immediately</li>
        <li>Not attempt to manage a serious safety situation alone without involving the appropriate authorities or services</li>
        <li>Document what happened as soon as it is safe to do so and report to the Executive team after the event</li>
      </ol>

      <Heading level="h2">8. Commitment and Reliability</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">8.1 Deadlines</Heading>
      <p>
        Staff are expected to meet the deadlines assigned to them. Consistent failure to meet deadlines undermines the club's ability to operate and puts more pressure on other staff members.
      </p>
      <p>If you cannot meet a deadline, you must:</p>
      <ol class="list-inside list-decimal space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Notify your Team Lead (or the relevant Executive if there is no TL) as early as possible</li>
        <li>Provide a realistic revised timeline</li>
        <li>Not wait until after the deadline has passed to raise the issue</li>
      </ol>

      <Heading level="h3">8.2 Event Rostering</Heading>
      <p>
        If you are rostered to assist at or run a DUCA event, follow these guidelines:
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Situation</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">What you must do</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">You will be late</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Contact the rostering Team Lead or relevant Executive as soon as you know you will be late.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">You cannot attend</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Find a confirmed replacement before pulling out, and notify your Team Lead or a relevant Executive.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">You need to pull out</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Give at least 24 hours' notice to the relevant Executive, and ensure a replacement is confirmed.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Emergency</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Please take care of yourself first. Contact an Executive as soon as you are able. A follow-up conversation will take place after the event.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-amber-400 block mb-2">⚠️ Attendance Responsibility</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-amber-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          You cannot simply not show up. If you are rostered and cannot attend, it is your responsibility to ensure coverage is arranged before you step back. Pulling out without securing a replacement and without adequate notice (except in an emergency) is a breach of this Code of Conduct.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h3">8.3 Emergency Pull-Outs</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA understands that genuine emergencies or sicknesses happen. If you need to pull out of a commitment due to an emergency:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Contact an Executive as soon as you are able to.</li>
        <li>A follow-up conversation with an Executive will take place after the fact to clarify details.</li>
        <li>The outcome of that conversation depends on the nature and circumstances of the emergency.</li>
        <li>No disciplinary action will be taken for genuine emergencies.</li>
      </ul>

      <Heading level="h2">9. Leadership and Initiative</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">9.1 At Events</Heading>
      <p>
        All DUCA staff are trusted to step up when needed. If you are the most senior DUCA person present at an event and an Executive is not available or reachable, you are expected to:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Keep the event running smoothly and in line with the planned format.</li>
        <li>Make decisions necessary to protect the safety and experience of attendees.</li>
        <li>Contact an Executive as soon as possible if a significant issue arises.</li>
        <li>Document what happened and report back to the Executive team after the event.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You do not need explicit permission to act in the interest of attendees and the club when a situation requires it.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">9.2 General Initiative</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA does not operate through micromanagement. Staff are trusted to use their judgment within their role. If you see something that needs doing and it falls within your scope, act on it. If you are not sure whether something is within your scope, ask before acting.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">10. Representing DUCA</Heading>
      <p>
        You represent DUCA whenever you are acting in your staff capacity, attending a DUCA event, engaging with a partner or sponsor on DUCA's behalf, or identifying yourself as a DUCA staff member. In all of these contexts:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Your conduct reflects on the club and its members.</li>
        <li>You must be professional, respectful, and consistent with DUCA's values.</li>
        <li>You must not make commitments or promises on behalf of DUCA without authorisation from the President.</li>
        <li>You must not publicly disparage DUCA, DUSA, Deakin University, or partner organisations.</li>
        <li>You must not represent your personal views as DUCA's position on any matter.</li>
      </ul>

      <Heading level="h2">11. Confidentiality and Privacy</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">11.1 Member Data</Heading>
      <p>
        Some staff roles involve access to member information, including names, contact details, and membership records. This information:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Must only be used for legitimate club purposes.</li>
        <li>Must not be shared outside the club without member consent or DUSA approval.</li>
        <li>Must not be used for personal benefit or passed to third parties.</li>
      </ul>

      <Heading level="h3">11.2 Internal Club Information</Heading>
      <p>
        Internal discussions, financial information, planning documents, and staff communications are confidential. Do not share these externally without Executive approval. This includes sharing content from internal Discord channels, staff meetings, or planning documents.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">11.3 After Your Role Ends</Heading>
      <p>
        Confidentiality obligations continue after you leave your role. You must not share internal club information, member data, or confidential club communications after your role ends.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">12. Financial Integrity</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">12.1 Club Funds and Resources</Heading>
      <p>
        All DUCA funds are held in the DUSA Club Account and managed by the Treasurer in accordance with DUSA's financial rules. Staff must not:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Use DUCA funds or resources for personal purposes.</li>
        <li>Make financial commitments on behalf of the club without President authorisation.</li>
        <li>Handle any cash collected at events without following the procedures set by the Treasurer.</li>
      </ul>

      <Heading level="h3">12.2 Conflicts of Interest</Heading>
      <p>
        If you have a personal, financial, or professional interest in a decision DUCA is making (for example, a vendor the club is considering has a connection to someone you know, or you would personally benefit from a decision), you must:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-inside list-decimal space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Disclose the conflict to the President or Treasurer before any decision is made.</li>
        <li>Remove yourself from any vote or decision-making process on that matter.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Failing to disclose a known conflict of interest is a serious breach of this Code.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">13. Raising Concerns and Formal Complaints</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">13.1 Your Right to Raise Concerns</Heading>
      <p>
        Every DUCA staff member has the right to raise concerns about their role, about the conduct of another person in the club, or about anything else affecting the club. DUCA will not take adverse action against any person for raising a concern in good faith.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">13.2 Leaving Your Role</Heading>
      <p>
        You can choose to step down from your role at any time. If you do:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Submit a written resignation to the President or Secretary.</li>
        <li>Give as much notice as possible to allow for handover.</li>
        <li>Complete or hand over any outstanding work before your last day.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        DUCA respects your right to leave and will work with you to ensure a clean transition.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">13.3 Formal Complaint Process</Heading>
      <p>
        If you have a complaint about the conduct of another staff member, follow the steps below:
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Step</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Action</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Step 1</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Raise the concern with your Team Lead or the relevant Executive Officer.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Step 2</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">The Executive acknowledges the complaint within 3 business days.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Step 3</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">A meeting is arranged between the relevant parties and a neutral Executive Officer.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Step 4</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">The outcome is documented and communicated to all parties.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Step 5</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">If the complaint is not resolved, or if the complaint is about an Executive, it is escalated to the President.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Step 6</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">If the complaint involves the President, or involves serious misconduct that cannot be resolved internally, it is escalated to DUSA.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-red-400 block mb-2">⚠️ Good Faith Complaints</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-red-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Complaints must be made in good faith. Raising a complaint that is knowingly false or intended to harm another person is itself a breach of this Code of Conduct.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h2">14. Unresponsiveness</Heading>
      <p>
        DUCA relies on all staff being contactable and responsive within reasonable timeframes. Staff who go dark without notice create risk for the team and for events.
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Stage</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">What Happens</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">1. Initial Absence</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Staff member is unresponsive to messages or assigned tasks. The relevant Executive or TL follows up directly.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">2. No Response</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">No response after a reasonable follow-up period. The staff member is called to a meeting with an Executive to discuss the situation.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">3. Redundancy</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">No engagement after the meeting. The staff member's role is reviewed and they may be made redundant.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        If you know you will be unavailable for an extended period (illness, travel, personal circumstances), let your Team Lead or a relevant Executive know in advance. DUCA will work with you. Unexplained silence is not acceptable.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">15. Disciplinary Process</Heading>

      <Heading level="h3">15.1 How Breaches Are Handled</Heading>
      <p>
        If a staff member acts in a way that goes against this Code of Conduct, the following process applies.
      </p>
      
      <p class="font-semibold text-white">Step 1: Meeting</p>
      <p>
        The staff member is called to a meeting with the President or the relevant Executive, depending on the nature and seriousness of the breach. The purpose of this meeting is to understand what happened and give the staff member an opportunity to respond.
      </p>
      
      <p class="font-semibold text-white">Step 2: Outcome</p>
      <p>One of the following outcomes will apply after the meeting:</p>

      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Outcome</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">When it applies</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">No action</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">The matter is resolved or the conduct does not meet the threshold for a formal breach.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Formal Breach & Written Warning</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">The conduct was a breach but does not warrant immediate dismissal.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Immediate Dismissal</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">The conduct is serious enough to warrant instant removal from the role.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-950/20 p-6 my-6">
        <strong class="text-red-400 block mb-2">⚠️ Written Warning Threshold</strong>
        <p class="text-sm text-red-200/90 leading-relaxed m-0">
          Two formal breaches result in automatic dismissal from the staff role, regardless of how much time has passed between them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Heading level="h3">15.2 Grounds for Immediate Dismissal</Heading>
      <p>
        The following conduct may result in immediate dismissal without a prior warning:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-inside list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Hate speech, discrimination, or conduct targeting a person based on any protected characteristic</li>
        <li>Violence, physical aggression, or threatening behaviour at or in connection with DUCA</li>
        <li>Serious financial misconduct, including theft, fraud, or deliberate misuse of club funds</li>
        <li>Serious harassment or bullying of a member, staff member, partner, or attendee</li>
        <li>Deliberate misrepresentation of DUCA that causes reputational or operational harm to the club</li>
        <li>Any conduct that places the safety of members, attendees, or staff at serious risk</li>
        <li>Serious breach of member data or confidentiality obligations</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This list is not exhaustive. The President and the advisory board reserve the right to determine that other conduct warrants immediate dismissal where the circumstances are sufficiently serious.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h3">15.3 Appeals</Heading>
      <p>If a staff member believes a disciplinary outcome is unfair, they may appeal:</p>
      <ol class="list-inside list-decimal space-y-1 pl-4">
        <li>Submit a written appeal to the President within 7 days of receiving the outcome.</li>
        <li>If the President was involved in the original decision, submit the appeal to a club advisor.</li>
        <li>A neutral advisory board member will review the appeal and communicate a decision within 14 days.</li>
        <li>If no neutral advisor is available, the matter may be escalated to DUSA for review.</li>
      </ol>

      <Heading level="h2">16. DUCA's Rights and Protections</Heading>
      <p>
        This section documents the rights DUCA reserves as an organisation to protect its members, its operations, and its standing.
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-950/20 text-left text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900/50 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-200">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Right</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4">Detail</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Right to remove staff</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">DUCA may remove any person from a staff role where they are found to have breached this Code of Conduct, following the process in Section 15.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Right to conduct reviews</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">DUCA may conduct social media or conduct reviews where a concern is raised about a current staff member.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Right to update this document</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">DUCA may update this Code of Conduct at any time. Staff will be notified of material changes and asked to re-acknowledge where appropriate.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Right to escalate externally</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Where a matter involves serious misconduct, financial fraud, or potential legal liability, DUCA may escalate directly to DUSA or other appropriate authorities.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Right to act in member interests</td>
              <td class="px-6 py-4">Where a staff member's conduct poses an immediate risk to the safety or wellbeing of members or attendees, DUCA may act immediately, including removing the person from an event, before completing the formal process.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        DUCA accepts that staff are individuals with personal lives, opinions, and circumstances that are not the club's business. This Code of Conduct does not attempt to govern every aspect of a staff member's private life. It governs conduct that affects the club, its members, its partners, and DUCA's ability to operate.
      </p>
      <p>
        DUCA commits to applying these standards consistently and fairly, without bias toward or against any individual.
      </p>

      <Heading level="h2">17. Acknowledgement</Heading>
      <p>
        All staff members must sign or digitally acknowledge this Code of Conduct upon accepting their role. Acknowledgement confirms that you have read, understood, and agreed to comply with these standards for the duration of your role.
      </p>
      <p>
        Failure to acknowledge this document does not exempt a staff member from the obligations it contains.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-slate-800 my-8" />
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 text-center">
        Deakin University Cybersecurity Association | DUCA Staff Code of Conduct | Version 1.0<br />
        This document is maintained by the DUCA President and reviewed annually.
      </p>
    </div>
